This document provides a detailed step-by-step guide for restoring multiple databases in phases, migrating logins and fixing orphaned users using dbatools.
1. Ensure PowerShell 5.1 or 7 is installed.
2. Install dbatools module:
Install-Module dbatools -Scope CurrentUser -AllowClobber -Force -SkipPublisherCheck
3. Verify connectivity to source and destination instances using Test-DbaConnection.

===========-================================= 
--COPYING LOGINS WITH POWERSHELL DBATOOLS 
--NOTE: always use full server name
---ExcludeLogin lets you skip specific logins from the copy operation—useful when you don’t want certain accounts (like an admin group you manage manually) to be copied or altered on the destination.

--IMPORT ALL LOGINS FROM SOURCE TO DESTINATION
Copy-DbaLogin -Source complete/servername -Destination complete/servername -ExcludeLogin OH\DBAteams -Force

--REPORT ORPHANUSER
Find-DbaOrphanUser -SqlInstance AGQL22R01 | Format-Table (OLD)
Get-DbaDbOrphanUser -SqlInstance 'complete/servername' | Format-Table --new

--CHECK THE ORPHAN USERS FIX 
Repair-DbaDbOrphanUser -SqlInstance 'complete/servername' -WhatIf -Verbose 

--FIX THE ORPHAN USERS 
Repair-DbaDbOrphanUser -SqlInstance 'complete/servername' -Verbose 

